rst step that uses the built-in browser, the browser pane inside the Claude desktop app (also called the in-app browser, the browser pane, Claude's browser, or \"your own browser\"), whose tools are named mcp__Claude_Browser__* when the session runs in the desktop app and mcp__remote-devices__Claude_Browser__* when a cloud session is linked to the person's computer; before those tools are turned on there may be a single enable__mcp__remote-devices__Claude_Browser tool instead. It covers the pane's persistent sign-ins, tabs and preview_start, reading pages as text, site approvals, what the pane cannot open, and what to do when it cannot be reached. It is not for Claude in Chrome (mcp__claude-in-chrome__* tools), which has its own skill, and it does not decide which browser to use.", "input": null, "name": "built-in-browser"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "chrome-browser", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/chrome-browser/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:chrome-browser", "scope": "user"}, "description": "Read this skill before the first step that uses Claude in Chrome, the browser extension whose tools are named mcp__claude-in-chrome__* (also called Chrome, the browser extension, or the external browser) and which acts in the person's real Chrome with their own sign-ins; before those tools are turned on there may be a single enable__mcp__claude-in-chrome tool instead. It covers loading the tools in one ToolSearch call, checking the person's open tabs and working in a new tab, site permissions, GIF recordings, console logs, dialogs to avoid, and when to stop and ask. It is not for the built-in browser (mcp__Claude_Browser__* or mcp__remote-devices__Claude_Browser__* tools), which has its own skill, and it does not decide which browser to use.", "input": null, "name": "chrome-browser"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "computer-use", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/computer-use/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:computer-use", "scope": "user"}, "description": "Read this skill before the first step of any request to do something in an app on the person's own computer (Notes, Finder, System Settings, any desktop app), to look at their screen, or for \"computer use\". Computer use (desktop control) lets Claude take screenshots of the person's desktop and control it with clicks, typing and scrolling through the Claude desktop app; its tools are named mcp__computer-use__* when the session runs in the desktop app and mcp__remote-devices__computer_* when a cloud session is linked to the person's computer; before computer use is turned on for a conversation there may be no such tools, only an enable__mcp__remote-devices__computer tool, which turns it on. It covers turning it on, picking the right tool, the access flow, and the safety rules for tiered apps, links and financial actions. It is not for websites, which go through Claude in Chrome or the built-in browser and their own skills.", "input": null, "name": "computer-use"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "deep-research", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/deep-research/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:deep-research", "scope": "user"}, "description": "Use this skill when the user's prompt requires (1) researching a topic across multiple sources, comparing options or alternatives, analyzing trends or history, understanding markets or industries, or reviewing literature or studies and (2) synthesizing that research into a comprehensive, narrative report. If you're planning to search the web or internal knowledge bases, consider using this skill. This skill coordinates research subagents, so use it only when you have a tool for spawning subagents (the Agent or Task tool); otherwise, research the question directly.", "input": null, "name": "user:deep-research"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "docs", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/docs/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:docs", "scope": "user"}, "description": "docs (editable docs people share and comment on; the default for any document, named as a doc or not: a document, report, proposal, resume, cover letter, letter, contract, policy, form, template, worksheet, essay, handbook, guide, how-to, cheat sheet, SOP or other writing to keep, share, collaborate on, send, submit, print or sign; a doc exports to Word, PDF, Markdown or Google Docs, so needing a file to send, attach, upload, submit or print is no reason to pick Word, and a file nobody asked for is a doc, not Word; a plan, comparison, summary or notes asked in chat stays in chat; a pasted claude.ai artifact link may be a doc: check with docs tools first; Word or another file format named, tracked changes wanted, or a .docx to change or use as a template → that format's skill): making one → if no docs-connector instructions are in context, call its `guide` (topic.instructions) first; then create the doc (headings only, no body) before any search, file read or plan, even with files attached.", "input": null, "name": "user:docs"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "google-workspace", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/google-workspace/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:google-workspace", "scope": "user"}, "description": "Read this before the first Google Drive, Docs, Sheets or Slides connector call whenever the task creates or changes a Google file. Use this skill whenever the user wants to create or change a Google Doc, Sheet or Slides file in their Google Drive. Triggers include: a request that names Google Docs, Sheets, Slides or Drive and asks to make, edit, format, copy or rename a file; a docs.google.com link with a request to change that file, even a one-line fix or suggested edits; and any follow-up change to a Google file from earlier in the chat, even \"change it\" or \"add a tab\". Includes helper scripts for document positions, cell ranges and slide layout. However, if the user asks for a doc, deck or spreadsheet without naming Google, or gives a Google file only as source material for something new, use Claude's own output type instead. Do NOT use for read-only questions about a Google file, or for Word, Excel, PowerPoint or PDF files.", "input": null, "name": "google-workspace"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "import-memory", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/import-memory/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:import-memory", "scope": "user"}, "description": "Import a memory export from another AI assistant into Claude's memory — conversationally, additively, and with the content treated as data.", "input": null, "name": "import-memory"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "morning", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.claude/skills/synced/361cf177-edaf-443d-9568-8fbe1f7d4ded_9b930875-b033-4f1b-b793-2e312c505c68/morning/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "user:morning", "scope": "user"}, "description": "Render the user's morning brief as a styled HTML artifact, or set it up as a recurring weekday task. Use only when the user explicitly asks to run, see, or set up their morning brief, or if they invoke /morning by name. A question about their day, schedule, or calendar is not by itself a request for the brief; answer it directly instead.", "input": null, "name": "morning"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "build-with-ai", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/build-with-ai/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:build-with-ai", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Build AI apps on SpaceXAI (XAI_API_KEY + api.x.ai)", "input": {"hint": "<what you're building>"}, "name": "build-with-ai"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "code-review", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/code-review/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:code-review", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Run an extremely strict maintainability review for abstraction quality, giant files, and spaghetti-condition growth. Use for a deep code quality audit or an especially harsh maintainability review.", "input": null, "name": "code-review"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "create-skill", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:create-skill", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Create a new Grok skill", "input": null, "name": "create-skill"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "create-workflow", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/create-workflow/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:create-workflow", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Author a new multi-agent workflow", "input": null, "name": "create-workflow"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "design", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/design/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:design", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Run the full design-doc-writer and design-doc-reviewer loop until consensus. Produces a polished design document with a PR plan.", "input": {"hint": "<description of what to design> [--publish]"}, "name": "design"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "execute-plan", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/execute-plan/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:execute-plan", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Execute a PR Plan DAG from a design document. Parses the plan, topologically sorts it, implements PRs in parallel using worktree-isolated subagents, runs mandatory orchestrator-level review, and assembles either a Graphite PR stack or a plain-git branch stack depending on tool availability.", "input": {"hint": "<design-doc-path> [--effort N] [--concurrency N] [--dry-run] [--resume <PLAN_ID>] [--instructions \"...\"] [--no-graphite] [--auto-pr]"}, "name": "execute-plan"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "game-assets", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/game-assets/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:game-assets", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Engine-ready game art, 2D sprites to 3D models", "input": null, "name": "game-assets"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "imagine", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/imagine/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:imagine", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Prompting and workflow guidance for Imagine image and video tools", "input": null, "name": "bundled:imagine"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "implement", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/implement/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:implement", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Run the full implement-review-fix loop using implementer and reviewer personas. Supports effort-based multi-reviewer scaling (2–7 reviewers) with automatic specialization selection. Includes memory-based feedback loop that learns from past review patterns. Loops until all reviewers find 0 issues of any severity.", "input": {"hint": "[--effort N] <description of what to implement>"}, "name": "implement"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "learn", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/learn/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:learn", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Learn from your own Grok Build sessions and tune your setup: add skills for things you keep typing, fix stale skill instructions, and retire skills, plugins, or MCP servers you never use. Use on \"/learn\", \"learn from my traces\", \"what skills do I never use\". Not for summarizing sessions into notes or memory.", "input": {"hint": "[--mode step|auto|report] [--days N | --since-last | --limit N] [--per-trace] [--include-headless] [--cwd PATH] [--focus TEXT] [--resume]"}, "name": "learn"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "long-running-background-tasks", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:long-running-background-tasks", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.", "input": null, "name": "long-running-background-tasks"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "pr-babysit", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/pr-babysit/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:pr-babysit", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Monitor PRs, fix CI failures, address review comments (human and bot/automated), resolve merge conflicts, and restack stacks. Supports independent PRs, Graphite stacks, and GitHub stacked PRs (gh-stack). Optional ship lands a ready PR bottom-up when every job has passed and no comments remain open.", "input": {"hint": "add [--ship] <number> | remove <number> | list | check | ship [on|off] [number...]"}, "name": "pr-babysit"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "resume-claude", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/resume-claude/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:resume-claude", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Continue from a recent Claude Code session", "input": {"hint": "[words describing the session | session id]"}, "name": "resume-claude"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "resume-codex", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/resume-codex/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:resume-codex", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Continue from a recent Codex session", "input": {"hint": "[words describing the session | session id]"}, "name": "resume-codex"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "resume-cursor", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/resume-cursor/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:resume-cursor", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Continue from a recent Cursor session", "input": {"hint": "[words describing the session | session id]"}, "name": "resume-cursor"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "review", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/review/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:review", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Run a reviewer subagent against your whole branch vs main, your uncommitted working state, a named branch, a single GitHub PR, or an entire Graphite/stacked-PR stack (one reviewer subagent per PR). A bare /review defaults to reviewing your uncommitted working state when the tree is dirty, or your whole branch vs main when the tree is clean. Main, local, and branch modes write a review file plus a summary to disk. PR and stack modes post the findings as a PENDING GitHub review for the user to inspect and submit through the UI. Use --main for an explicit clean-tree branch review, --stack for stacked PRs, --submit to publish immediately as COMMENT, or --approve to publish and approve; the default remains PENDING.", "input": {"hint": "[--main | --local | --branch <name> | --pr <number-or-url> | --stack <number-or-url> | <auto-detect>] [--approve | --submit]"}, "name": "review"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "skill-design-principles", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/skill-design-principles/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:skill-design-principles", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Concise, high-signal principles for writing and editing skills well. Use whenever authoring or editing a skill.", "input": null, "name": "skill-design-principles"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "statusline", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/statusline/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:statusline", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Configure the Grok Build status line.", "input": null, "name": "statusline"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "threejs-frame-conventions", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/threejs-frame-conventions/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:threejs-frame