ort] [--days N | --since-last | --limit N] [--per-trace] [--include-headless] [--cwd PATH] [--focus TEXT] [--resume]"}, "name": "learn"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "long-running-background-tasks", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:long-running-background-tasks", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.", "input": null, "name": "long-running-background-tasks"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "pr-babysit", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/pr-babysit/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:pr-babysit", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Monitor PRs, fix CI failures, address review comments (human and bot/automated), resolve merge conflicts, and restack stacks. Supports independent PRs, Graphite stacks, and GitHub stacked PRs (gh-stack). Optional ship lands a ready PR bottom-up when every job has passed and no comments remain open.", "input": {"hint": "add [--ship] <number> | remove <number> | list | check | ship [on|off] [number...]"}, "name": "pr-babysit"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "resume-claude", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/resume-claude/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:resume-claude", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Continue from a recent Claude Code session", "input": {"hint": "[words describing the session | session id]"}, "name": "resume-claude"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "resume-codex", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/resume-codex/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:resume-codex", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Continue from a recent Codex session", "input": {"hint": "[words describing the session | session id]"}, "name": "resume-codex"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "resume-cursor", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/resume-cursor/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:resume-cursor", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Continue from a recent Cursor session", "input": {"hint": "[words describing the session | session id]"}, "name": "resume-cursor"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "review", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/review/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:review", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Run a reviewer subagent against your whole branch vs main, your uncommitted working state, a named branch, a single GitHub PR, or an entire Graphite/stacked-PR stack (one reviewer subagent per PR). A bare /review defaults to reviewing your uncommitted working state when the tree is dirty, or your whole branch vs main when the tree is clean. Main, local, and branch modes write a review file plus a summary to disk. PR and stack modes post the findings as a PENDING GitHub review for the user to inspect and submit through the UI. Use --main for an explicit clean-tree branch review, --stack for stacked PRs, --submit to publish immediately as COMMENT, or --approve to publish and approve; the default remains PENDING.", "input": {"hint": "[--main | --local | --branch <name> | --pr <number-or-url> | --stack <number-or-url> | <auto-detect>] [--approve | --submit]"}, "name": "review"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "skill-design-principles", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/bundled/skills/skill-design-principles/SKILL.md", "qualifiedName": "bundled:skill-design-principles", "scope": "bundled"}, "description": "Concise, high-signal principles for writing and editing skills well. Use whenever authoring or editing a skill.", "input": null, "name": "skill-design-principles"}, {"_meta": {"bareName": "statusline", "path": "/Users/ylmacstudio/.grok/b